{
  "mn59:0.1": "Middle Discourses 59 ",
  "mn59:0.2": "The Many Kinds of Feeling ",
  "mn59:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn59:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn59:1.3": "Then the chamberlain Pañcakaṅga went up to Venerable Udāyī, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "mn59:1.4": "“Sir, how many feelings has the Buddha spoken of?” ",
  "mn59:1.5": "“Chamberlain, the Buddha has spoken of three feelings: ",
  "mn59:1.6": "pleasant, painful, and neutral. ",
  "mn59:1.7": "The Buddha has spoken of these three feelings.” ",
  "mn59:1.8": "When he said this, Pañcakaṅga said to Udāyī, ",
  "mn59:1.9": "“Sir, Udāyī, the Buddha hasn’t spoken of three feelings. ",
  "mn59:1.10": "He’s spoken of two feelings: ",
  "mn59:1.11": "pleasant and painful. ",
  "mn59:1.12": "The Buddha said that neutral feeling is included as a peaceful and subtle kind of pleasure.” ",
  "mn59:2.1": "For a second time, Udāyī said to Pañcakaṅga, ",
  "mn59:2.2": "“The Buddha hasn’t spoken of two feelings, ",
  "mn59:2.3": "he’s spoken of three.” ",
  "mn59:2.4": "",
  "mn59:2.5": "",
  "mn59:2.6": "For a second time, Pañcakaṅga said to Udāyī, ",
  "mn59:2.7": "“The Buddha hasn’t spoken of three feelings, ",
  "mn59:2.8": "he’s spoken of two.” ",
  "mn59:2.9": "",
  "mn59:2.10": "",
  "mn59:3.1": "And for a third time, Udāyī said to Pañcakaṅga, ",
